      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Architectural Mismatch / Functional Regression**\n\nThe `fp_command_vendor` handler populates `args-\u003eoutput_buf` and sets `args-\u003eoutput_buf_size` (indicating it returns a dynamically sized response). However, `EC_HOST_CMD_HANDLER_REQ_ONLY` declares to the upstream framework that this command only expects request data and has no response struct. In Zephyr limits, this may constrain the allocated maximum response buffer bound to `0`, leading to truncations or memory corruption when the handler writes to it (whereas the old `DECLARE_HOST_COMMAND` expanded to `EC_HOST_CMD_HANDLER_UNBOUND` which permitted dynamic responses).\n\nPlease use `EC_HOST_CMD_HANDLER_UNBOUND(EC_CMD_FP_VENDOR, fp_command_vendor, EC_VER_MASK(0))` or a similar appropriate macro that permits generating a response. [🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8465043_30548198-9bcd-468f-b70d-31a73260838f.pb)",
